      "headline": "NATO Secretary General Rutte visits Prague, presses Babi\u0161 on defense spending; government excludes President Pavel from Ankara summit delegation",
      "summary": "NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte made an unannounced visit to Prague on April 16, meeting with PM Babi\u0161 over Czech defense spending, which the government counts differently than NATO methodology and falls below the 2% GDP threshold. Babi\u0161 pledged to fulfill commitments but offered no binding numbers. Simultaneously the government quietly approved army aircraft allocations for the July Ankara summit covering only Babi\u0161, Foreign Minister Macinka, and Defense Minister Z\u016fna \u2014 omitting President Pavel, who insists on attending under his constitutional prerogatives. The dispute between Babi\u0161 and Pavel escalated into a major political controversy, with opposition criticism and commentary across Czech and Slovak outlets.",
